# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=conquest spec=druid:feral
# style=mash view=844x390,touch save=fresh.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl and every .play under playtest/plans/ first: `mash`
# has never been run on any battleground before, on any map. direction.md's
# #7 ("a battleground does not carry a passive body the way a raid does")
# has flee/dodge (zero presses, never steers), good/melee (steers + presses,
# dies in ~9-15s on every map tried so far) and auto (no steering at all,
# presses only what the bar allows -- mostly nothing, since nobody walks
# into range). `mash`'s own steering branch is missing entirely from
# scripts/playbot.ts's want-computation (only dodge/good/melee/wander/flee/
# learn compute a `want`), so mash releases the stick and stands exactly
# where it is for the whole match while round-robining ability slots 1-5 --
# a body that is maximally active with its buttons and totally inert with
# its feet. That's a different corner from anything #7 has on record: not
# "never fights" (dodge/flee) and not "fights then dies fast" (good/melee on
# a melee spec that beelines into the enemy cluster) but "fights whatever
# wanders into range, from a fixed spot, forever." Feral druid is melee, so
# if nothing ever comes to it, mash should read identically to dodge/flee on
# the output side (hits=0) despite being constantly pressing -- worth
# checking bill for exactly that.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
targets
shot bg-menu

tap map:conquest
targets
shot conquest-picked

tap class:druid:feral
shot class-picked

tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play mash 90
shot mid1
state
bill
says

wait 5
play mash 90
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play mash 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
